const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文研究机器学习方法如何用于资产定价中的条件预期收益与特征关系建模。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhaa009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源把多个机器学习模型置于统一的资产定价训练、验证和评估安排中，而不是只展示一个模型的拟合值。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhaa009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要带日期的特征、收益、证券样本、退市处理、训练验证测试划分、调参记录和可得性时钟。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhaa009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"研究讨论模型在历史样本和评估设计中的表现；复杂模型的拟合或变量重要性并不自动给出经济因果解释。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhaa009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"严格隔离训练与测试，保存全部候选模型和调参过程，按当时可得信息处理特征，并纳入退市与样本成员变化。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhaa009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (2020)。该论文不提供实时预测服务或可执行组合；历史机器学习结果不能替代成本、容量和分布变化评估。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (2020) for “Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhaa009",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2020) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。该论文不提供实时预测服务或可执行组合；历史机器学习结果不能替代成本、容量和分布变化评估。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
